    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5b916234-1104-534d-ac67-68d2fd551fc0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Simplify.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{9}\\right)}{\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\right)}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $s=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\right)$ and $c=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\right)$. The **double-angle formula** gives $\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{9}\\right)=2sc$.\n\n Also, $\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\right)=\\frac{s}{c}$.\n\nRewrite the quotient ratio before cancelling.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2sc}{\\frac{s}{c}} &=2c^2 \\\\ &=2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{18}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll cancellations use nonzero factors in the original expression.",
